{"causes":["Mao's rise to power in the Chinese Communist Party led to the establishment of the People's Republic of China in 1949.","The Chinese Civil War, which ended with the Communist victory, reshaped the country's politics, economy, and society.","The Soviet Union's policies and ideologies influenced Mao's vision for a socialist China."],"effects":["The Quotations became a central text of the Cultural Revolution, shaping the ideology and actions of the radical movement.","Mao's statements influenced Chinese education, with the Quotations being widely taught in schools and universities.","The collection's emphasis on revolutionary fervor and the importance of the people contributed to the radicalization of Chinese politics in the 1960s and 1970s."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"mao-zedong","sourceName":"Mao Zedong","verb":"CREATES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao Zedong compiled the Quotations from his speeches and writings."},{"sourceSlug":"chinese-people","sourceName":"Chinese people","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"The Chinese people widely disseminated and referenced Mao's statements, making them an integral part of their cultural heritage."},{"sourceSlug":"cultural-revolution","sourceName":"Cultural Revolution","verb":"OCCURS_DURING","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"The Cultural Revolution marked a period of intense ideological and political fervor, during which the Quotations played a central role."},{"sourceSlug":"china","sourceName":"China","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao's statements and ideology shaped China's domestic and foreign policies during the 1960s and 1970s."},{"sourceSlug":"socialist-china","sourceName":"Socialist China","verb":"DEFINES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao's Quotations are often seen as a defining text of Socialist China, encapsulating its core ideology and values."},{"sourceSlug":"cultural-revolution","sourceName":"Cultural Revolution","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"The Cultural Revolution, which was closely tied to Mao's ideology, was shaped by the Quotations' emphasis on revolutionary fervor and the importance of the people."},{"sourceSlug":"china-communist-party","sourceName":"China Communist Party","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao's statements and ideology have had a lasting impact on the Chinese Communist Party's policies and ideology."},{"sourceSlug":"china-society","sourceName":"China Society","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao's Quotations have had a profound impact on Chinese society, shaping its values, norms, and cultural practices."},{"sourceSlug":"chinese-education","sourceName":"Chinese education","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"The Quotations have been widely taught in Chinese schools and universities, shaping the country's educational system and curriculum."},{"sourceSlug":"socialist-education","sourceName":"Socialist education","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung","targetName":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","context":"Mao's Quotations have had a lasting impact on the development of socialist education in China, shaping its curriculum and pedagogy."}],"places":[{"name":"Beijing, China","role":"Major center of publication and dissemination"},{"name":"Shanghai, China","role":"Key location for the compilation and printing of the Quotations"},{"name":"Mao's hometown, Shaoshan, China","role":"Birthplace and childhood home of Mao Zedong"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung","type":"Reference article","slug":"quotations-from-chairman-mao-tse-tung"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q36393","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quotations_from_Chairman_Mao_Tse-tung"],"tags":["literary work","Historical & Literary Texts","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung contributed to the historical record of the Classical period. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.","summary":"Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung (Chinese: 毛主席语录, Máo Zhǔxí Yǔlù, 'Quotations from Chairman Mao'), widely known as the Little Red Book (小红书), is a collection of brief quotations from speeches and writings of Mao Zedong (1893–1976), Chairman of the Communist Party of China, compiled and published by the People's Liberation Army under the direction of Lin Biao (Mao's Defence Minister) and first distributed within the military in 1964. A mass civilian edition was published in 1966 at the start of the Cultural Revolution, and the book subsequently became the most published book in the history of the world: an estimated 5–6.5 billion copies were printed during the Cultural Revolution (1966–1976), making it by some measures the second most printed book after the Bible.

The Little Red Book contains 427 quotations from Mao's writings and speeches, organised by subject in 33 chapters covering topics such as the Communist Party, classes in Chinese society, the mass line, war and peace, imperialism, criticism and self-criticism, party discipline, and the cultural revolution. The quotations range from strategic political analysis to aphoristic wisdom, and the book was designed for easy memorisation and recitation: its physical format — small red vinyl cover, pocket-sized, with bold headings and short quotations — facilitated its use as a handbook for political education and as a ritual object in Cultural Revolution practice.

During the Cultural Revolution, possession and constant reference to the Little Red Book was mandatory across China — reciting passages, 'studying' the book in group sessions, and waving it at political rallies were obligatory practices. The book's status as a quasi-sacred text of Communist China — used for collective oath-taking, displayed in homes and workplaces, and treated with near-religious reverence — made it one of the defining objects of 20th-century political culture and a paradigm case of the state-directed production of a political sacred text.","subjects":["Chinese Literature","Modern Era","Mao Zedong","Chinese Communism","Cultural Revolution","Political Text","20th Century","Chinese History"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS","CAUSE_AND_EFFECT"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"The Quotations from Chairman Mao Tse-tung played a significant role in shaping the ideology and actions of the Cultural Revolution, and have had a lasting impact on Chinese politics, education, and culture.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
